# Third-party notices and attribution

This repository integrates and builds on work by others. The project would not
exist without it.

## o3root — the temporary root chain (MIT)

  https://github.com/zsw125/o3root

`apps/o3root/jniLibs/arm64-v8a/libo3p.so` is the unmodified payload built from
o3root v3.0. It implements the CVE-2026-98260 privilege escalation and the
runtime KernelSU LKM loader that this project's root flow drives. All credit for
that exploit chain belongs to the o3root authors. Our own code only drives it
(Shizuku), stages it, patches SELinux policy with ksud, and runs the NPU probes.

o3root is MIT licensed. Its own disclaimer applies: research/education only,
run it on hardware you own, expect crashes, and treat the result as a
research-grade root, not a production one.

## KernelSU (GPL-3.0)

  https://github.com/tiann/KernelSU

`ksud` is extracted from the KernelSU manager APK at build time
(`scripts/fetch-ksud.sh`) and is **not** redistributed here. The KernelSU LKM
itself is embedded inside the o3root payload.

## Shizuku (Apache-2.0)

  https://github.com/RikkaApps/Shizuku

`tools/shizuku/*.jar` are the client libraries used to run the payload in the
`shell` SELinux domain.

## llama.cpp (MIT)

  https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp

`tools/ggml-o3npu/` is a ggml backend plugin for llama.cpp; llama.cpp itself is
not vendored here.

## Vendor libraries

The VeriSilicon / Xiaomi NPU userspace libraries (`libxnumd.so`, `libxnnl.so`,
`libovxlib.so`, ...) are proprietary and are **not** redistributed. The tools
here load them from the device at runtime, or from files you pull yourself.
